# Core

- Read `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/README.md` before editing.
- Demo issue → read `no-push/runs/` first (last 3). Graphify query only for architecture questions not already in this chat. No `--update` unless the user asked or a local query missed.
- Gemini / graphify LLM: never, unless local extract failed.
- Shortest working diff. Reuse existing code. No speculative files.
- No decorative comments. Comment only non-obvious constraints.
- Handle loading and error states at IO, network, and UI boundaries.
- Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Generated by`, or any AI authorship.
- Local extracts and scratch go in `no-push/`. Never stage that folder.
- New code module → add `docs/modules/<name>.md` in the same change.
- `CONTEXT.md` is glossary only. Architecture lives in `docs/`.
